@startuml
 title Resumefolio - Evidence-based validation states
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #17324D
}
state "Assumption record" as Assumption {
  state "Unverified" as AUnknown
  state "Confirmed" as AConfirmed #DCFCE7
  state "Invalidated" as AInvalidated #FEE2E2
  [*] --> AUnknown
  AUnknown --> AConfirmed : evidence supports expectation
  AUnknown --> AInvalidated : evidence contradicts expectation
  AConfirmed --> AUnknown : conditions or evidence change
  AInvalidated --> AUnknown : revised assumption needs validation
}
state "Dependency record" as Dependency {
  state "Unverified" as DUnknown
  state "Available" as DAvailable #DCFCE7
  state "Blocked" as DBlocked #FEE2E2
  [*] --> DUnknown
  DUnknown --> DAvailable : required use verified
  DUnknown --> DBlocked : required prerequisite unavailable
  DAvailable --> DUnknown : scope or conditions change
  DAvailable --> DBlocked : access or required service lost
  DBlocked --> DUnknown : new evidence needs reassessment
}
legend bottom
Every status change needs evidence, an owner and a review point.
Partial tool success does not validate the full application dependency set.
No actual item status is changed by this diagram.
endlegend
@enduml
